{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1229769-circle-of-the-crone-worshipping-things-from-changeling-the-hedge-rather-than-spirits","id":1229769,"title":"Circle of the Crone worshipping things from Changeling/The hedge rather than spirits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-24T02:52:43-07:00","id":1229769,"title":"Circle of the Crone worshipping things from Changeling/The hedge rather than spirits?","content":"Was just musing recently, as I read through the Circle of the Crone covenant book. So the Circle often worship Spirits, and they have a big interest in the natural world. So if a Hierophant got a glimpse of the Hedge in some way, what are the chances it could lead to a Circle cult that worships fae entities the way others worship spirits?<br /> <br /> I don't really know anything about Changeling other than what some friends and a quick browsing of the wiki have taught me, so I'm wondering if any of you have done something like this in the past, or if those of you who have actually played/read Changeling could see how it could fit together?<br /> <br /> (Maybe this should have gone in the Changeling sub-forum? Really hard to tell with a topic like this.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T04:08:58-07:00","id":1229776,"title":"","content":"It's a thread about a vampire thing that also requires knowledge of a changeling thing so I think it's the right forum.<br /> As for worshipping hedge denizens, I think that could work. My interpretation is that spirit worship is relatively uncommon (partly due to VTR never including spirit rules so it can't be the default way of playing the game) and stumbling upon the hedge is even less common. But if Acolytes with a penchant for worshipping entities beside the Crone stumbles upon the Hedge, then there's definitely grounds for at least veneration of the realm.<br /> The question (that I don't feel comfortable to answer due to my own lacking experience with CTL) is exactly what type of entities that would be fitting to worship. True Fae seems somewhat farfetched since they're all the way in Arcadia, and any second hand accounts won't likely portray them positively. Or maybe it's exactly their negative portrayal that makes them enticing to the Acolytes. Perhaps even considered an alternative take on the Crone herself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T04:30:29-07:00","id":1229778,"title":"","content":"You've got my creative juices flowing. The realm itself could be the subject of worship. Perhaps they could not enter it physically, but could reach out to it with their consciousness by performing certain rituals at a particular doorway into the hedge, and enter spiritually, treating it as a spirit journey, a divine &quot;vision&quot;, interpreting what they see as oracular wisdom and cryptic messages from the beyond.<br /> <br /> Considering how dangerous the Hedge and its inhabitants can be, it paints the theme of &quot;Tribulation is Enlightenment&quot; in a rather literal and visceral way. Perhaps on these voyages the consumption of certain Goblin Fruits could lead to actual visions or temporary insights. The glade where these grow could require a dangerous trip from the point of entry to where this particular type grows (eating the wrong type could be... bad/interesting), all the while a ritual is underway around the one doing the spirit quest to keep the connection up (this ritual being interrupted would leave the central ritual subject's spirit lost on the other side and needing to find its way back on its own, which would be... bad/interesting). It could be the ritual you need to take for Initiation out of the Chorus. One example of one such initiation in the book is a trip through the woods to a certain glade, with the woods being werewolf territory. This seems like an interesting parallel.<br /> <br /> This can just be one ritual practice the Circle undertakes, with perhaps one or two more centred around the Hedge out of their total package of ritual practices, but it doesn't need to be specifically a &quot;Hedge Cult&quot;. Just like spirits tend not to be the whole of a cult's worship, but rather one of their many practices tied into their specific form of worship. In the case of this cult, it would be one with a high level of devotion towards nature, seeing the Hedge as a sort of mystical expression of nature itself, perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 06-24-2018, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T11:43:06-07:00","id":1230062,"title":"","content":"I'll start by admitting that my knowledge of Circle practices is thin. That said, the impression is that they are 1) omnivorous when it comes to &quot;pagan&quot; worship practices regional or otherwise and, 2) venerate more broadly the thread of maiden/mother/crone female goddess motifs with special focus on the Crone part. These are also not exclusive points, nor are they ones that VtR comments on as to their &quot;correctness&quot; as a results-oriented belief structure--Circle adepts get results because of Cruac at minimum and no one really knows why Cruac works.<br /> <br /> That said, the practices of Circle worship and Cruac are BOTH likely to attract the attention of supernatural Others, who could benefit from the release of energy (Vitae/blood/Glamour) and/or take an interest in the clear avenues for manipulation a coven might present. Thus: spirits. Also, Hedge Denizens and even True Fae. <br /> <br /> Keep in mind it's not that the True Fae don't like &quot;Ironside&quot;--they just need a good reason to get involved and bear the cost of either manifesting or drawing creatures closer to them (Hedge, at minimum). They also have very, very long associations with the themes and iconography that flow from the triune-goddess myths and especially so in the British Isles where it seems the Circle <i>codified</i> itself first. (I'm perhaps wrong on this point.)<br /> <br /> Were I a bored True Fae, manipulating a coven of ecstatic vampires into serving me would sound like a fun diversion and potentially useful source of mortals (Changelings) and/or tools; you could easily employ them as a Loyalist troupe, or a wrecking ball against a Court that offended. Plus all the delicious story and emotions vamps generate....<br /> <br /> Side note: In my own campaign arc there are several very old characters who purposefully are blurred between vampire and Fae. Notably this includes The Morrigan, a vampiric manifestation, and within the Fae court the entities Anand, Macha, Badb and Fea/Nemain. In other words, I want to have my story cake and eat it too. The handwaving involves these as genuine people at one point, who ended up cursed vampires AND passed under the hills with the rest of the Tautha to become part of the Fae; diablerie may or may not have occurred to create The Morrigan. Really, defining this stuff down too far takes the spook out.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T12:30:34-07:00","id":1230083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1229769-circle-of-the-crone-worshipping-things-from-changeling-the-hedge-rather-than-spirits?p=1230062#post1230062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll start by admitting that my knowledge of Circle practices is thin. That said, the impression is that they are 1) omnivorous when it comes to &quot;pagan&quot; worship practices regional or otherwise and, 2) venerate more broadly the thread of maiden/mother/crone female goddess motifs with special focus on the Crone part. These are also not exclusive points, nor are they ones that VtR comments on as to their &quot;correctness&quot; as a results-oriented belief structure--Circle adepts get results because of Cruac at minimum and no one really knows why Cruac works.<br /> <br /> That said, the practices of Circle worship and Cruac are BOTH likely to attract the attention of supernatural Others, who could benefit from the release of energy (Vitae/blood/Glamour) and/or take an interest in the clear avenues for manipulation a coven might present. Thus: spirits. Also, Hedge Denizens and even True Fae.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind it's not that the True Fae don't like &quot;Ironside&quot;--they just need a good reason to get involved and bear the cost of either manifesting or drawing creatures closer to them (Hedge, at minimum). They also have very, very long associations with the themes and iconography that flow from the triune-goddess myths and especially so in the British Isles where it seems the Circle <i>codified</i> itself first. (I'm perhaps wrong on this point.)<br /> <br /> Were I a bored True Fae, manipulating a coven of ecstatic vampires into serving me would sound like a fun diversion and potentially useful source of mortals (Changelings) and/or tools; you could easily employ them as a Loyalist troupe, or a wrecking ball against a Court that offended. Plus all the delicious story and emotions vamps generate....<br /> <br /> Side note: In my own campaign arc there are several very old characters who purposefully are blurred between vampire and Fae. Notably this includes The Morrigan, a vampiric manifestation, and within the Fae court the entities Anand, Macha, Badb and Fea/Nemain. In other words, I want to have my story cake and eat it too. The handwaving involves these as genuine people at one point, who ended up cursed vampires AND passed under the hills with the rest of the Tautha to become part of the Fae; diablerie may or may not have occurred to create The Morrigan. Really, defining this stuff down too far takes the spook out.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>My campaign will be set in Victorian England, as it so happens, so &quot;especially in the British Isles' peaks my interest. You seem to have experience with Changeling, could you tell me what parts of their core splatbook (or a supplement if it would do a better job) I'd need to read to understand the link to triune-goddesses and such? As well as maybe how and for what reasons True Fae may interact with &quot;Ironside&quot;?<br /> <br /> As a response to your side note: I think you are right when it comes to not defining everything. The CoD books themselves do this all the time, as well. The unknown is just scarier, mechanics provide a way players can quantify the supernatural and thus focuses their impulses away from fear and towards &quot;Ok, let me mathhammer what it would take to beat this...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T15:11:28-07:00","id":1230105,"title":"","content":"The CoC is an alliance of polytheistic faiths that share Cruac, so the beings they worship, study, and make deals with can vary from region to region, some might focus on spirits, others True Fey, others Ghosts, others Cruac created blood gods, and others weirder things, it was very diverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T20:26:58-07:00","id":1230169,"title":"","content":"Would like more info on Cruac Blood God's<br /> <br /> seems kind of pointless as is.<br /> <br /> Oh one Cruac Ritual Im having Trouble with <br /> <br /> <br /> Pool of Forbidden Truth's<br /> <br /> Can the Altar Merit Benefit the final dice pool on it, as it isnt standard.<br /> <br /> 2nd Can it be used on anothers behalf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T21:40:28-07:00","id":1230186,"title":"","content":"I see the Crone and Cruac as being more more closely linked to the Strix, but a Strix who somehow became a Goblin Queen would be a dope antagonist.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-2/posts/2171940\" target=\"_blank\">Also, obligatory link/reminder is obligitory</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T04:55:57-07:00","id":1230239,"title":"","content":"Speaking of reminders, &quot;The Danse Macabre&quot; supplement introduced Children of the Thorns, who worhip some Hedge entity. They're not technically the Circle, but spiritually? They fit perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T06:00:35-07:00","id":1230252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1229769-circle-of-the-crone-worshipping-things-from-changeling-the-hedge-rather-than-spirits?p=1230083#post1230083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My campaign will be set in Victorian England, as it so happens, so &quot;especially in the British Isles' peaks my interest. You seem to have experience with Changeling, could you tell me what parts of their core splatbook (or a supplement if it would do a better job) I'd need to read to understand the link to triune-goddesses and such? As well as maybe how and for what reasons True Fae may interact with &quot;Ironside&quot;?<br /> <br /> As a response to your side note: I think you are right when it comes to not defining everything. The CoD books themselves do this all the time, as well. The unknown is just scarier, mechanics provide a way players can quantify the supernatural and thus focuses their impulses away from fear and towards &quot;Ok, let me mathhammer what it would take to beat this...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had a long and elaborate response typed out that evaporated and haven't the heart to recompose at the moment.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say that True Fae can and will imitate the legends of, well, faerie. They will order themselves and compete among themselves according to rules that they set (no challenge can be completely impossible, for example), and they need the real world to fill the creativity gap that they have. There is a lot of conjecture as to where the True Fae came from, other than &quot;Changelings with high Wyrd&quot;, but to me it makes sense to assume that mortals/supernaturals that dabble in the Hedge long enough could slip into their roles over time--literally becoming the gods and legends mortals know.<br /> <br /> If you really want to become all-powerful and eternal (on par with ascending), becoming True Fae is the way to go. It's not that simple of course, but it is <i>nearly</i> so, and you'd not understand the difference until it's too late.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> in relation to the thread, the Blood God ritual would be <i>perfect </i>for creating a vessel to be filled by a coven's specific spiritual or otherworldly entity. In that respect the point is not to create some super-powerful monster you only vaguely control, but to create something into which the monster you bow to can call home (temporarily, anyway). This doesn't exclude enacting the ritual for other purposes, of course.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> how about the Welsh legend of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blodeuwedd\" target=\"_blank\">Blodeuwedd</a>? She was literally made by magic out of flowers and such to be the wife of someone, who quite casually betrays him after falling into lust with a visitor, and then is ultimately (re-?)turned into an owl. This is one that I'm going to use as a secondary antagonist, tapped by an unwise NPC Weihan Cynn member in a bid for revenge against a PC. Following the rules of &quot;define lightly&quot; all I know is that Blodeuwedd has the ability to create Hedge gates and once there sports access to the shape-changing magic of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Math_fab_Mathonwy\" target=\"_blank\">Math fab Mathonwy</a>, has contacts with Fae, wants a body again, and is linked to vices of lust. She's probably a Goblin Queen, but I'm waiting on the upcoming Changeling 2e release to define further.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T11:22:19-07:00","id":1230331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1229769-circle-of-the-crone-worshipping-things-from-changeling-the-hedge-rather-than-spirits?p=1230239#post1230239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of reminders, &quot;The Danse Macabre&quot; supplement introduced Children of the Thorns, who worhip some Hedge entity. They're not technically the Circle, but spiritually? They fit perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea, thanks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div c