-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> in relation to the thread, the Blood God ritual would be <i>perfect </i>for creating a vessel to be filled by a coven's specific spiritual or otherworldly entity. In that respect the point is not to create some super-powerful monster you only vaguely control, but to create something into which the monster you bow to can call home (temporarily, anyway). This doesn't exclude enacting the ritual for other purposes, of course.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> how about the Welsh legend of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blodeuwedd\" target=\"_blank\">Blodeuwedd</a>? She was literally made by magic out of flowers and such to be the wife of someone, who quite casually betrays him after falling into lust with a visitor, and then is ultimately (re-?)turned into an owl. This is one that I'm going to use as a secondary antagonist, tapped by an unwise NPC Weihan Cynn member in a bid for revenge against a PC. Following the rules of &quot;define lightly&quot; all I know is that Blodeuwedd has the ability to create Hedge gates and once there sports access to the shape-changing magic of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Math_fab_Mathonwy\" target=\"_blank\">Math fab Mathonwy</a>, has contacts with Fae, wants a body again, and is linked to vices of lust. She's probably a Goblin Queen, but I'm waiting on the upcoming Changeling 2e release to define further.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf </div> </div> </div>Weihan Cynn is from Requiem for Regina, right? Funnily enough, I have just earlier today learned this exists and just picked it up to see if I want to run in Elizebethan times instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T12:15:05-07:00","id":1230343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1229769-circle-of-the-crone-worshipping-things-from-changeling-the-hedge-rather-than-spirits?p=1230331#post1230331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weihan Cynn is from Requiem for Regina, right? Funnily enough, I have just earlier today learned this exists and just picked it up to see if I want to run in Elizebethan times instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. The Weihan Cynn are interesting, and I'm sure that there would be a few around in Elizabethian times--though most would have moved on to more vital Covenants.<br /> <br /> My understanding of the Cynn is that they represented a web of occulted knowledge of supernatural contacts: what exists, roughly where, how to contact them, what they wanted and what they might offer. They shared this knowledge more-or-less freely within the Covenant (boons aside), and then members went out and cultivated relationships with supernaturals (e.g. werewolves, spirits, Changelings... True Fae...) in order to accomplish things they couldn't or wouldn't do through their fellow vamps.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting idea, and certainly could if exercised judiciously leave ones' fellow, highly paranoid vampires feeling like touching the Cynn amounted to buying trouble in large, weird doses.<br /> <br /> <b>Fun bit:</b> the name appears to mean &quot;Holy/Sacred Tribe/People&quot;, which could both refer to how they saw themselves, as sacred intermediaries between mortals/vamps and &quot;other&quot; entities, and as their assumed function as a type of vampiric priestly caste in the Isles. Isles, or beyond, to Germany. I say this because the words are proto-Germanic and NOT of British origin. This implies that perhaps the Weihan Cynn came over with the Germanic foederati of the 3rd and 4th centuries, or the &quot;Saxon&quot; invasions of the 5th century. If they did not, then by elimination we could surmise the Covenant was reorganized by either invading vamps or at least those embraced from the Germanic invaders--probably around the late 6th century when British resistance largely collapsed.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 06-26-2018, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}